WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.625
The tooth on the hollow copper tool turns the front drive disc. Its lug still has room to move.

00:00:02.625 --> 00:00:05.000
The lug meets the carrier stop. As the carrier starts to turn, the housing pushes the sidebar against the rear disc.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.250
The silver tip passes through the copper tool. The front and middle discs turn easily while the rear disc carries the load.

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:09.167
The rear disc takes more effort to turn because its rim is rubbing against the sidebar.

00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:09.750
The notch in the rear disc reaches the sidebar. The bar moves into the notch until the middle disc stops it. The picker can now feel the resistance at the middle disc.

